@startuml poll-review
' cumin works - the Reviewer request (I3), and the way out of cumin/status/reviewing that every poll and the end of a Reviewer run decide (I5, I6, I7, I8, I10).
' Document: poll.md, section on the Reviewer request.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:I3: every required check passed on the head commit;
:Read the login of the Reviewer App
and the last cumin/status/ready of the issue;
:Count the round from the reviews on GitHub
(pure function);
:Write the head commit and zero counts
of requests to the state file;
:Change the label to cumin/status/reviewing;
:Remove the Reviewer worktree,
open the head commit detached;
if (Round?) then (1)
  :New session;
else (2 or later)
  :Resume the Reviewer session;
  :Name the last reviewed commit;
endif
if (The Reviewer approved an earlier commit?) then (yes)
  :Name the last approved commit
  (round 1: review only the diff from it);
else (no)
endif
:Run the Reviewer ("review");
note right
  blocked: change the label, write the comment,
  notify the Owner (row I10).
  Done and abnormal end: the way out below decides.
  Not started: the count stays; the second time,
  hand back to the Owner (row I3 or I8).
  cumin stops after its runs: the end of the run
  starts no request, and changes no label.
end note
partition "The way out of cumin/status/reviewing: every poll, and the end of a Reviewer run" {
  if (A Reviewer runs for the issue?) then (yes)
    :Change nothing, read nothing;
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  :Read the issue again, with the facts:
  who added the label and when, the question comments,
  the last cumin/status/ready, the state file;
  if (The label is of cumin-core or of an Owner?) then (no)
    :Do nothing; tell the Owner once;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Decide with the pure function ReviewEnd;
  if (A question comment after the label?) then (yes)
    :I10: change the label to cumin/status/awaiting-decision;
    :Notify the Owner;
  elseif (The head commit moved?) then (yes)
    :Change the label to cumin/status/checking
    (the old review still counts as a round);
  elseif (Review on the head commit?) then (APPROVE)
    if (DecideMerge?) then (risk/low)
      :I6: the merge procedure;
    elseif (risk/medium or risk/high) then
      :I7: change the label to
      cumin/status/awaiting-merge-decision;
      :Notify the Owner once;
    elseif (a required check does not pass) then
      :Change the label to cumin/status/checking;
    else (not exactly one risk label)
      :Hand back to the Owner (row I6);
    endif
  elseif (REQUEST_CHANGES) then
    if (Round below max_review_rounds?) then (yes)
      :I5: change the label to cumin/status/implementing;
      :Ask the Implementer to fix the comments
      (its own session, the branch of the pull request);
    elseif (A decision request of the Reviewer
    after its last review?) then (yes)
      :I8: change the label to cumin/status/awaiting-decision;
      :Notify the Owner (link: that comment);
    elseif (The cause was just requested with done,
    or requested twice in this stay?) then (yes)
      :Hand back to the Owner (row I8);
    elseif (Quota at a limit?) then (yes)
      :Request nothing, count nothing;
    else (no)
      :Count the request in the state file;
      :I8: ask the Reviewer to explain the cause
      (the same session);
    endif
  else (none)
    if (Requested again in this stay?
    (count in the state file)) then (yes)
      :Hand back to the Owner (row I5,
      after an abnormal end: with its kind);
    elseif (Quota at a limit?) then (yes)
      :Request nothing, count nothing;
    else (no)
      :Count the request in the state file;
      :Ask the Reviewer once more
      (after a done run: the short text in its session,
      at a poll or after an abnormal end:
      the whole review request);
    endif
  endif
}
stop
@enduml
